  "header": "Agents gain reach — and expose the cost of acting without guardrails",
  "friendlyHeader": "AI agents can do more, so they need stronger limits",
  "summary": "Today’s issue is about AI moving beyond answers into real work: investigating threats, running browser experiments, training specialist models, coordinating research and changing interfaces on demand. Two security incidents also make the counterpoint clear: useful autonomy needs scoped access, human checkpoints and fast detection when an agent crosses a boundary.",
